 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Train YOLOv8 Gun Detector (Colab-ready)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook installs dependencies, mounts Google Drive, validates the dataset layout, and trains a YOLOv8 detector for the gun dataset. Follow cells in order."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1) Install dependencies\n",
    "Installs ultralytics and other minimal packages. Colab will provide CUDA-enabled PyTorch by default on GPU runtimes." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install ultralytics and helpers\n",
    "!pip install -q ultralytics==8.4.116 pyyaml\n",
    "# (Optional) upgrade if needed: !pip install -q -U ultralytics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Check GPU and PyTorch CUDA support"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "print('torch', torch.__version__)\n",
    "print('cuda available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        print('device name:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print('cuda device name error:', e)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Mount Google Drive and set dataset path\n",
    "Place your dataset folder (the entire `Gun with webcam views.v1i.yolov8` folder) into Drive at the path you choose, e.g. `MyDrive/strix_datasets/Gun_with_webcam_views`. Then set DATASET_DRIVE_PATH accordingly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "# Point this to where you uploaded the dataset in Drive (example):\n",
    "DATASET_DRIVE_PATH = 'MyDrive/strix_datasets/Gun_with_webcam_views'  # <--- set this to your Drive path\n",
    "!mkdir -p /content/dataset\n",
    "# Copy or unzip if needed (if you uploaded a zip, uncomment unzip commands)\n",
    "# Example if you uploaded a zip to Drive:\n",
    "# !unzip -q '/content/drive/MyDrive/strix_datasets/Gun_with_webcam_views.zip' -d /content/dataset\n",
    "# Or copy the folder directly from Drive to /content/dataset:\n",
    "!rsync -av --progress "/content/drive/{0}/" /content/dataset/ || true".format(DATASET_DRIVE_PATH)
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4) Inspect dataset and data.yaml\n",
    "Show the tree and validate data.yaml contents." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!ls -la /content/dataset | sed -n '1,200p'\n",
    "# show data.yaml if present\n",
    "import yaml, os\n",
    "cfg_path = '/content/dataset/data.yaml'\n",
    "if os.path.exists(cfg_path):\n",
    "    with open(cfg_path) as f:\n",
    "        cfg = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
    "    print('data.yaml:')\n",
    "    print(cfg)\n",
    "    # Basic validation\n",
    "    if 'nc' in cfg and 'names' in cfg:\n",
    "        if cfg['nc'] != len(cfg['names']):\n",
    "            print('WARNING: nc != len(names)')\n",
    "        print('Classes:', cfg['names'])\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('No nc/names found in data.yaml; please verify format')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('data.yaml not found at /content/dataset/data.yaml; please ensure dataset is copied correctly')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5) Optional: merge person dataset (COCO) with gun dataset\n",
    "This is optional. If you want a single model detecting both person and gun, merge datasets and remap class ids so: person=0, gun=1. The commands are commented and need manual verification before running." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# OPTIONAL: merge datasets (commented).\n",
    "# Steps (high level):\n",
    "# 1) Prepare a target folder /content/dataset_merged with images and labels subfolders\n",
    "# 2) Copy all images and labels from COCO-person dataset and reindex/rename if needed\n",
    "# 3) Copy gun dataset images and labels, remap gun class id from 0 to 1 in its label files\n",
    "# 4) Create data.yaml with names: ['person', 'gun'] and correct train/val/test paths\n",
    "# Example snippet to remap gun labels to class 1 (use carefully):\n",
    "# import os\n",
    "# for label_file in gun_label_files:\n",
    "#     lines = open(label_file).read().splitlines()\n",
    "#     new_lines = []\n",
    "#     for L in lines:\n",
    "#         parts = L.split()\n",
    "#         parts[0] = '1'  # remap gun class 0 -> 1\n",
    "#         new_lines.append(' '.join(parts))\n",
    "#     open(label_file,'w').write('\n'.join(new_lines))\n",
    "# After merging, create /content/dataset_merged/data.yaml with: names: ['person','gun'] and proper paths." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6) Training - quick test and full training cells\n",
    "Choose quick test first (epochs=5, imgsz=320) to validate, then run full (epochs=50, imgsz=640)." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Quick test: small run to validate everything (use device=0 for GPU)\n",
    "# Adjust 'project' or --name to avoid overwriting runs\n",
    "!yolo task=detect mode=train model=yolov8n.pt data=/content/dataset/data.yaml epochs=5 imgsz=320 batch=8 device=0 name=colab_quick_test\n",
    "\n",
    "# Full run recommendation (uncomment to run):\n",
    "# !yolo task=detect mode=train model=yolov8n.pt data=/content/dataset/data.yaml epochs=50 imgsz=640 batch=16 device=0 name=colab_full_run\n",
    "# If OOM reduce batch to 8 or imgsz to 512" 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7) After training: locate best.pt and copy to Drive\n",
    "The trained weights are in runs/detect/<name>/weights/best.pt. Copy them back to Drive so you can download and use in your project." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: copy best.pt back to Drive (adjust run name)\n",
    "RUN_NAME = 'colab_full_run'  # change to your run name\n",
    "src = f'/content/runs/detect/{RUN_NAME}/weights/best.pt'\n",
    "dst = f'/content/drive/MyDrive/strix_models/{RUN_NAME}_best.pt'\n",
    "import os\n",
    "if os.path.exists(src):\n",
    "    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    !cp {src} {dst}\n",
    "    print('Copied to', dst)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('best.pt not found at', src)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8) Test / Inference on a sample image\n",
    "Run inference with the trained weights and show results inline." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Path to a sample image in dataset (adjust as needed)\n",
    "SAMPLE_IMG = '/content/dataset/train/images/'  # set to an actual image path\n",
    "# Example inference using the ultralytics Python API\n",
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "import glob, os\n",
    "# find an example image\n",
    "imgs = glob.glob('/content/dataset/**/images/*.*', recursive=True)\n",
    "if imgs:\n",
    "    img0 = imgs[0]\n",
    "    print('Running inference on', img0)\n",
    "    # use trained weights if available, else fallback to yolov8n.pt\n",
    "    weights = '/content/runs/detect/colab_full_run/weights/best.pt'\n",
    "    model_path = weights if os.path.exists(weights) else 'yolov8n.pt'\n",
    "    model = YOLO(model_path)\n",
    "    res = model(img0)
    
" 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display predictions (save and show image)\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "# save result to file and display\n",
    "out_path = '/content/pred.jpg'\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    res[0].plot(save=True, fname=out_path)\n",
    "    display(Image(out_path))\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print('Inference/plot error:', e)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9) How to update your project (app/detection.py) after export\n",
    "After you download the trained weights to your project, update the detector to use the new model and disable simulation." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example instructions to run locally after copying best.pt into your project models/ folder:\n",
    "print('1) Copy best.pt to your project, e.g. app/models/gun_best.pt')\n",
    "print('2) In app/detection.py set:')\n",
    "print("   model_path = 'app/models/gun_best.pt'")\n",
    "print('   WEAPON_CLASS_IDS = [0]  # single-class gun dataset -> class 0')\n",
    "print('   SIMULATE_SECOND_PERSON_AS_WEAPON = False')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10) Troubleshooting tips\n",
    "- OOM: reduce batch or imgsz, or use smaller model (yolov8n).\n",
    "- Use mixed precision (Ultralytics uses AMP on GPU automatically).\n",
    "- If labels look wrong, inspect label .txt files: each line is `class x_center y_center w h` normalized.\n",
    "- If you want final accuracy improvements: more epochs, better augmentations, larger model (yolov8s/m) and run on stronger GPU."
   ]
  }
